---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Why kprobe exists and where kernel-level forensics fits in production debugging."
>
  <div class="page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="section-label">about</div>
        <h1>kprobe is a flight recorder for the layer your APM cannot see.</h1>
        <p>
          Modern observability explains application behavior. kprobe explains
          what the Linux kernel did underneath it: scheduling, syscalls, memory
          pressure, TCP timing, and the causal chain that connects those events
          to a failed request.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/docs" class="btn-primary">Read the docs</a>
          <a href="/compare" class="btn-secondary">Compare the gap</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="signal-panel" aria-label="kprobe positioning summary">
        <div class="signal-row">
          <span>captures</span>
          <strong>kernel events</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-row">
          <span>joins with</span>
          <strong>trace context</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-row">
          <span>outputs</span>
          <strong>causal graph + replay</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="compact-grid">
        <div class="story-card">
          <div class="section-label">why it exists</div>
          <h2>The hard incidents happen below your code.</h2>
          <p>
            A slow span can be a slow service, a scheduler delay, a memory
            reclaim storm, or a TCP retransmit. Application tools see the
            symptom. kprobe records the system events that explain the cause.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="story-card muted">
          <div class="section-label">where it fits</div>
          <h2>It complements your observability stack.</h2>
          <p>
            Keep Datadog, Prometheus, Jaeger, and OpenTelemetry. kprobe extends
            them downward into the host, then maps kernel events back to the
            services, pods, traces, and transactions engineers already use.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">positioning</div>
      <div class="positioning-grid">
        <div class="pos-card pos-card-is">
          <h2>kprobe is</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>A passive kernel event recorder</li>
            <li>A causal inference engine</li>
            <li>An incident replay system</li>
            <li>A debugging layer for platform teams</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="pos-card">
          <h2>kprobe is not</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>A replacement for APM or metrics</li>
            <li>A generic dashboarding platform</li>
            <li>A threshold alerting tool</li>
            <li>Useful without Linux host visibility</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">principles</div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="principle">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Observe without changing the app</h3>
          <p>No SDK, import, sidecar, or redeploy. The recorder attaches at the kernel.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Explain cause, not just sequence</h3>
          <p>Events become inspectable edges so engineers can see why a request failed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Turn incidents into test cases</h3>
          <p>Replay preserves the production event timeline so fixes can be tested against reality.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-label">built on</div>
      <div class="stack-strip">
        <span>Rust + Aya</span>
        <span>Go</span>
        <span>Kafka</span>
        <span>ClickHouse</span>
        <span>Neo4j</span>
        <span>Kubernetes</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page {
    width: 100%;
  }

  section {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero {
    min-height: auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 320px;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    padding-top: 4rem;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 660px;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 660px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3.25rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }

  .hero p,
  .story-card p,
  .principle p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero p {
    max-width: 560px;
    font-size: 0.975rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .btn-primary,
  .btn-secondary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 36px;
    padding: 0.55rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--button-text-on-accent);
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .btn-secondary:hover {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    border-color: var(--text-muted);
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
  }

  .signal-panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .signal-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .signal-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .signal-row span {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .signal-row strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .compact-grid,
  .positioning-grid,
  .principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .story-card,
  .pos-card,
  .principle {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .story-card.muted,
  .pos-card:not(.pos-card-is) {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  .story-card h2,
  .pos-card h2 {
    max-width: 520px;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .pos-card ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pos-card li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .pos-card li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65rem;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .principles {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .principle span {
    display: block;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .principle h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .principle p {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .stack-strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .stack-strip span {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .signal-panel,
    .story-card,
    .pos-card,
    .principle,
    .stack-strip span {
      transition:
        background-color var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard),
        border-color var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard),
        transform var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard),
        box-shadow var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard);
    }

    .story-card:hover,
    .pos-card:hover,
    .principle:hover,
    .stack-strip span:hover {
      transform: translateY(-1px);
      background: var(--bg-elevated);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 940px) {
    .hero,
    .compact-grid,
    .positioning-grid,
    .principles {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero {
      gap: 2rem;
      min-height: auto;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    section {
      padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      align-items: stretch;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .btn-primary,
    .btn-secondary {
      width: 100%;
    }
  }
</style>
